units of product 1 short, a loss of about 1,100.\n- **Candidate 4:** also cut on days 4 and 6, roughly 70 units of product 1 short.\n- **Candidate 2:** its small early product 1 orders let it get through day 4, but day 6 is still cut (about 41 units instead of 83). That is a shortfall of about 42 units, worth about 550.\n- **Daily ordering costs the same as ordering every other day.** Daily ordering pays 26 more in fixed fees every other day. Ordering every other day pays about 26 more in holding at the same rate. So the difference comes down to cash cuts and order sizes.\n- **Daily plans:**\n  - Candidate 5 orders the least early on and has no cut at all.\n  - Candidate 7 also gets through without a cut.\n  - Candidate 6 loses about 4 units of product 1 on day 4.\n  - Candidate 3 orders the most (about 1.1–1.15× forecast). It loses about 25 units of product 1 on day 4, but its larger orders pay off later because average demand runs about 4.6% above forecast.\n\n**Effect of randomness:** if early demand falls short of forecast, revenue drops and the cash cuts get deeper. That hits the plans with large early orders hardest (0, 1, 4). The daily plans spread payments out and hold up better.\n\nThe least certain calls are candidate 3 against candidate 2, and candidate 5, which under-orders product 1 early on."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5042, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5042}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:38:55.498Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWE18FnfPGcdKNfFqFgF"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, 